<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  The pad that edits one field of the online panel (the name, or the room code): a modal Screen canvas like Setup, hidden here, layer 33, over the panel
  Online (32). There is no text field in the engine, so the field is typed on keys. EntryValueRow shows the caption of the field (EntryCaptionName or
  EntryCaptionCode, one at a time) and its text ({onlineEntryValue}); PadKey0..47 are the keys, eight to a row PadRow0..5 (action MahjongOnlineKey, value the index;
  the character of key i is {padKey<i>}). The model decides how many keys the pad has (the room code 32, a name up to 44) and the component hides the keys and
  the rows it does not use, so the keys left share the plate; with all 48 shown the plate is full. EntryDelete (MahjongOnlineBackspace) removes the last character,
  EntryDone (MahjongOnlineDone) goes back to the form. EntryPaste (MahjongOnlinePaste, between them) is shown for the room code only: it reads the clipboard and
  fills the code; the shortcut Ctrl+V / Cmd+V does the same without it. EntryNote, one line under EntryValueRow ({onlineEntryNote}), is shown only while a paste has
  said something ("No room code in the text", "Nothing to paste", "Cannot paste here. Type the code"); the room code pad has 32 keys, four rows, so the two empty rows
  leave room for it, and the name pad (48 keys) never shows it. A key is flex 1 of its row with the row's height, so a row of fewer keys shows wider ones.
  The same pad also edits the tester's nickname (MahjongOnlineComponent, the page Options; EntryCaptionNickname is its caption), with the keys of a name.
  The plate is at most 544 high (32 padding + 56 value band + 6 x 56 pad rows + 64 actions + 7 x 8 spacing) and the rows share the height by flex weights at their
  maximum; the smallest canvas (320 x 320 units, 297 of safe height) leaves a row about 26 units and a key 25 units wide, both above the 21.3 units of 32 px, which is
  why the keys stay eight to a row in every window and nothing scrolls. The variants are those of Online: at most 480 units wide the plate takes the whole safe
  width and the captions are 52, at most 360 they are hidden. A key's character is one letter, so MahjongHudOnlineTest asks it to fit with 4 units of air, not 8.
  The skin is that of Online: the plate a card, EntryValueRow the header band, the keys radius 8 with no shadow (they lie 4 apart), EntryDelete, EntryPaste and EntryDone the buttons of their role.
-->
